# keur quality control — OS / editor junk file committed.
#
# Why this exists: guide items #6..#7 — .DS_Store (macOS), Thumbs.db (Windows),
# and per-user editor state leak into commits via `git add .`. They reveal the
# author's OS/editor, clutter diffs, and occasionally carry local paths. Not a
# security defect, so WARN.
#
# NOTE: directory-based junk (node_modules/, dist/, build/, __pycache__/) is not
# covered here — file-presence matches a file's BASENAME/extension, not a path
# segment, so "any file under node_modules/" needs a path-segment match the
# engine does not yet have. Tracked as a follow-up (a `path_contains` target or a
# dir-presence engine). This rule covers the exact-basename junk the engine can
# match reliably today.
#
# @see the "never commit" guides (.DS_Store, Thumbs.db, editor state).
id: KEUR-QUAL-008
title: OS / editor junk file committed
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: file-presence
action: warn
target:
  filenames: .DS_Store Thumbs.db desktop.ini .netrwhist
  extensions: .swp .swo
  exclude_paths: eval/corpus/repos/ vendor/ build/ dist/
message: "OS/editor junk committed (.DS_Store, Thumbs.db, editor state). Remove it and add to .gitignore (ideally a global core.excludesfile) — it clutters diffs and leaks local environment detail. @see KEUR-QUAL-008"
confidence: 0.7
fix: "Remove the file and add it to .gitignore. For machine-wide junk, set a global ignore once: add .DS_Store/Thumbs.db to ~/.gitignore_global and run 'git config --global core.excludesfile ~/.gitignore_global'."
